        "original_id": "71d8425a-5fbc-5e3b-adc4-edeb0d9489b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Maryland Jockey Club\n- Places: Pimlico Race Course, Laurel Park Racecourse, Bowie Race Track, Baltimore, Laurel, Bowie, Prince George's County, Maryland\n- People: Chick Lang, Sr.\n- Roles: businessman, general manager\n\nFacts:\n- The Maryland Jockey Club remains the corporate name of the company that operates Pimlico Race Course, Laurel Park Racecourse, and Bowie Race Track after 267 years.\n- Pimlico Race Course in Baltimore, Maryland, opened in 1870.\n- Laurel Park Racecourse in Laurel, Maryland, opened in 1911.\n- Bowie Race Track in Bowie, Maryland, opened as a race course in 1914.\n- Bowie Race Track ceased operations as a track in 1985.\n- Charles John \"Chick\" Lang, Sr. was born in 1926.\n- Bowie grew from a small railroad stop to become the largest municipality in Prince George's County, the fifth most populous city in Maryland, and the third largest Maryland city by area.\n- Charles John \"Chick\" Lang, Sr. was an American businessman and the general manager of the Maryland Jockey Club.\n- Charles John \"Chick\" Lang, Sr. died on March 18, 2010.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
